    "title": "LSU beats Arkansas in College World Series Semifinals, 6-5 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "BATON ROUGE, La. (Louisiana First) — The LSU Tigers held off the Arkansas Razorbacks in the College World Series Semifinals, 6-5. The Tigers advance to the CWS Championship Series against the Coastal Carolina Chanticleers. View updates of the game below. Zac Cowan is LSU’s starting pitcher, and Landon Beidelschies is Arkansas’ starting pitcher in tonight’s matchup. Top of the 1st (ARK): Bottom of the 1st (LSU): End of the 1st (0-0) Top of the 2nd (ARK): Bottom of the 2nd (LSU): End of the 2nd Inning (0-0) 3rd Inning Top of the 3rd (ARK): Bottom of the 3rd (LSU): End of the 3rd (0-0) Top of the 4th (ARK): Bottom of the 4th (LSU): End of the 4th (1-0) ARK Top of the 5th (ARK): Bottom of the 5th (LSU): End of the 5th Inning (1-0) Top of the 6th (ARK): Bottom of the 6th (LSU): End of the 6th (2-1) LSU Top of the 7th (ARK): Bottom of the 7th (LSU): End of the 7th Inning (2-1) Top of the 8th (ARK): Bottom of the 8th (LSU): End of the Inning (3-3) Top of the 9th (ARK): Bottom of the 9th (LSU): Final (6-5) LSU For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Louisiana First News.",
